selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#the-moody-diagram\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">The Moody Diagram<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#the-moody-diagram\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>The Moody diagram relates the Darcy friction factor, <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(f\\)</span>, to Reynolds number\nand relative surface roughness. Pyskyfire uses this friction factor when it\ncalculates pressure loss in a cooling channel.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/index.html#module-pyskyfire\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>pyskyfire - A Python library for rocket engine simulation and design.</p>", "a[href=\"#selecting-the-friction-backend\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Selecting the friction backend<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#selecting-the-friction-backend\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>This chart illustrates the <strong><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluids</span></code> backend for straight ducts</strong>, including\npyskyfire\u2019s smooth transition policy. It is a representative Moody chart, not a\nvalidation envelope or a plot of the native transition interpolation.\n<strong><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">native</span></code> remains the default</strong> for existing simulations and validation cases;\nselecting <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluids</span></code> is explicit.</p><p>For regenerative cooling, pass <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">friction_model=\"fluids\"</span></code>:</p>", "a[href=\"#straight-ducts-direct-branches-and-smooth-transition\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Straight ducts: direct branches and smooth transition<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#straight-ducts-direct-branches-and-smooth-transition\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluids</span></code> backend calls the upstream branch functions directly. The laminar\nbranch is</p>", "a[href=\"#native-backend-retained-for-validation\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Native backend retained for validation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#native-backend-retained-for-validation\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The native backend keeps its existing equations: <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(64/Re\\)</span> below 2300, a linear\nlaminar/turbulent blend from 2300 to 3500, and a turbulent result above 3500.\nFor smooth walls it uses <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\((0.79\\ln Re-1.64)^{-2}\\)</span>; for nonzero roughness it\nsolves Colebrook with <strong>3.71</strong>, rather than the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluids</span></code> value of 3.7. The native\nrough-wall numerical solve uses bracketed <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">brentq</span></code> in <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(z=1/\\sqrt{f}\\)</span> instead of\nunconstrained <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fsolve</span></code> in <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(f\\)</span>:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/coupled_solver/index.html#pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.coupled_steady_heating_analysis\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.coupled_steady_heating_analysis\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">coupled_steady_heating_analysis</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">thrust_chamber</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">boundary_conditions</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">nodes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">circuit_index</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">film</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'auto'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">film_model</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/coupled_solver/FilmHeatFluxModel.html#pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.FilmHeatFluxModel\" title=\"pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.FilmHeatFluxModel\"><span class=\"pre\">FilmHeatFluxModel</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">h_liquid_wall</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Callable</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">DEFAULT_H_LIQUID_WALL</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">film_x_array</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Sequence</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">solver</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'newton'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">output</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">heat_curvature_correction</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">pressure_curvature_correction</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">friction_model</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'native'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/coupled_solver/RegenResult.html#pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.RegenResult\" title=\"pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.RegenResult\"><span class=\"pre\">RegenResult</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>Run a steady heating analysis with film cooling, regen cooling, or both.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#correlation-warnings-and-applicability\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Correlation warnings and applicability<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#correlation-warnings-and-applicability\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.FrictionCorrelationWarning</span></code> is the exported warning category\nfor finite curved evaluations outside these documented conditions:</p>", "a[href=\"#how-the-chart-is-generated\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">How the chart is generated<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#how-the-chart-is-generated\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.PlotMoodyDiagram</span></code> calls\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.darcy_friction_factor(...,</span> <span class=\"pre\">model=\"fluids\")</span></code>. By default it\nsamples 400 logarithmically spaced Reynolds numbers from <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(7\\times10^2\\)</span> to\n<span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(10^8\\)</span> and explicitly includes both straight transition bounds, 2040 and\n<span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(2040(3500/2300)\\approx3104.35\\)</span>. There is no NaN plotting gap: each roughness\ncurve continuously displays the implemented smooth blend. The chart sets\n<span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(D_h=1\\)</span> so the absolute roughness value equals the relative roughness\n<span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(\\epsilon/D_h\\)</span>. The displayed Reynolds-number span is a plotting choice, not a\nvalidation range.</p><p>Generate <strong>only</strong> the Moody HTML artifact from the repository root:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/coupled_solver/RegenResult.html#pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.RegenResult\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.RegenResult\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.coupled_solver.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">RegenResult</span></span></dt><dd><p>Regenerative-cooling result with optional film-cooling data.</p><p>The coolant-state fields (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">coolant_enthalpy</span></code> onwards) describe the bulk\ncoolant along the circuit. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">coolant_enthalpy</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">coolant_quality</span></code> are\nall-<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">nan</span></code> when the coolant fell back to the temperature march, and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">coolant_quality</span></code> is <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">nan</span></code> at any station outside the boiling dome \u2013\nincluding supercritical stations, where no dome exists. Use\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">coolant_phase</span></code> to tell those cases apart.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/index.html#module-pyskyfire.ducts\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.ducts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.ducts\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Duct hydraulics shared by cooling channels, piping and manifolds.</p><p>This subpackage contains shared path geometry, explicit pipe hydraulics,\nannular ducts, orifices and orifice plates, and volute and collector manifolds. It depends only on <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/common/index.html#module-pyskyfire.common\" title=\"pyskyfire.common\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.common</span></code></a> for\nplanar section primitives and friction correlations and <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/index.html#module-pyskyfire.thermo\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo</span></code></a> for fluid state records,\nand it does not import from <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/index.html#module-pyskyfire.regen\" title=\"pyskyfire.regen\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen</span></code></a> or <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/network/index.html#module-pyskyfire.network\" title=\"pyskyfire.network\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network</span></code></a>,\nso cooling channels, turbopump hardware and engine-network adapters can all\ndepend on it without a cycle.</p>", "a[href=\"#quantities-in-the-diagram\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Quantities in the diagram<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#quantities-in-the-diagram\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The Reynolds number based on hydraulic diameter is</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/common/friction/index.html#pyskyfire.common.friction.darcy_friction_factor\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.common.friction.darcy_friction_factor\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.common.friction.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">darcy_friction_factor</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">ReDh</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Dh</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roughness</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">model</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'native'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">laminar_factor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Return the Darcy friction factor for a straight duct.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#curved-ducts-schmidt-correlations\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Curved ducts: Schmidt correlations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#curved-ducts-schmidt-correlations\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The straight-duct Moody chart does not include curvature. With\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pressure_curvature_correction=True</span></code>, the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluids</span></code> backend calls the forced\nSchmidt branch functions directly: <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">helical_laminar_fd_Schmidt</span></code> and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">helical_turbulent_fd_Schmidt</span></code>. It obtains the curved critical Reynolds number\nfrom <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">helical_transition_Re_Schmidt</span></code>. Here <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(D_i=D_h\\)</span> is the\nhydraulic-diameter substitution for the channel and <span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(D_c=2|R|\\)</span> is the coil\ndiameter measured between tube centerlines. The sign of the centerline radius\ndoes not affect friction. Schmidt\u2019s transition criterion is</p>", "a[href=\"regenerative-cooling-explanation.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Regenerative Cooling<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#regenerative-cooling\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>This page explains the regenerative cooling model implemented in <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen</span></code>. It traces the path through <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">coupled_solver.py</span></code>, shows how the solver calls the equations in <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">physics.py</span></code>, and explains how the hot-gas aerothermodynamic properties are prepared by <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo.aerothermodynamics</span></code>.</p><p>The model is a quasi-one-dimensional steady heat-exchanger calculation. At each axial station, it balances three heat-transfer paths:</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
